1.14.m:
Vāyu said:
And one should not, having come [to this stage] by knowledge, perform action out of passion;
for having experienced [the fruit of an action that is] passionate or dark, he is bound right there.

1.20.m:
The single syllable 'Om' is Brahman, the state deposited in the cave [of the heart].
This [syllable] 'Om' is the three Vedas, the three worlds, the three fires;
these are the three strides of Viṣṇu, and the Ṛg, Sāman, and Yajus verses.

And this is especially characterized by identical sovereign power;
for yogins especially, in the sovereign power possessing eight marks,
known as aṇimā and the rest, therefore the twice-born should apply it.
